                "text": "<p>First, Henry VIII married Anne Boleyn in 1533 after breaking with Rome to divorce his first wife, Catherine of Aragon. The Pope refused to recognise this divorce, meaning devout Catholics believed Catherine was still Henry’s lawful wife when Elizabeth was born. In 1536 Henry executed Anne Boleyn and passed an Act declaring Elizabeth illegitimate.</p><p>Second, the succession worried politicians when twenty-five-year-old Elizabeth became queen in November 1558. She was unmarried and had no Protestant child to inherit the throne if she died suddenly from illness. Consequently, her Privy Councillors and MPs in Parliament immediately urged her to choose either an English nobleman or a foreign prince as a husband.</p>",
