                "score": "3 / 12 Marks",
                "level": "Level 1 (Simple Statements)",
                "text": "<p>Elizabeth made her religious settlement a middle way in 1559 so that Catholics and Protestants would stop arguing with each other. England was also scared that France might invade if she changed the Church too much, so she tried to keep both sides happy.</p>",
                "verdict": "Level 1 (3/12) — Simple general points; needs specific Tudor facts, dates (e.g. 'Supreme Governor', 1559 Prayer Book, 12d recusancy fines), and 'because / this meant that' explanation."
