          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> Imprisoned on an island fortress at **Lochleven** Castle in July 1567, Mary was forced by rebel Protestant lords to abdicate in favour of her one-year-old son James VI under the regency of her Protestant half-brother, the **Earl of Moray**. In May 1568 Mary escaped Lochleven, raised 6,000 supporters, lost at Langside, and fled by fishing boat across the Solway Firth into England.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> Mary’s arrival trapped Elizabeth in an acute diplomatic dilemma. Sending English troops to restore a deposed Catholic monarch would alienate friendly Protestant Scotland; handing Mary back risked executing an anointed sovereign; allowing her abroad risked French military intervention; keeping her under **house arrest** inside England invited endless domestic Catholic plots.",
