                "level": "Level 2 (Stimulus-Bound Cap)",
                "text": "<p>One reason Mary, Queen of Scots was executed in 1587 was the Babington Plot in 1586. Anthony Babington planned for six Catholic gentlemen to murder Elizabeth and rescue Mary from captivity with foreign help. Mary wrote secret letters back agreeing to the plan to assassinate Elizabeth and replace her as queen.</p><p>Another reason was Walsingham’s spies. Sir Francis Walsingham used double agent Gilbert Gifford to intercept Mary’s coded letters that were hidden inside beer barrels at Chartley Manor. His codebreaker Thomas Phelippes decoded the letters proving Mary agreed to the plot, so Mary was put on trial at Fotheringhay Castle and executed.</p>",
