          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> Too late to rally support for the northern rebels, Pope Pius V issued the papal bull **Regnans in Excelsis** in February 1570, formally excommunicating Elizabeth as a heretic and commanding English Catholics to end their allegiance to her. Overnight, every devout English Catholic became a potential traitor in Parliament’s eyes, prompting the harsh **1571 Treasons Act** outlawing papal bulls.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> In 1571 Italian-born Florentine banker Roberto Ridolfi organised the international **Ridolfi Plot**: Philip II promised 10,000 Spanish troops under Alba to invade England, assassinate Elizabeth, and place Mary Stuart on the throne married to Norfolk. Cecil and Walsingham intercepted Ridolfi’s coded letters, leading directly to the **Duke of Norfolk**’s execution for high treason in June 1572.",
