          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> In 1586 young Derbyshire Catholic gentleman Anthony Babington organised the **Babington Plot** to murder Elizabeth at court, rescue Mary Stuart from Chartley Hall in Staffordshire, and trigger a joint Franco-Spanish Catholic invasion of 60,000 troops backed financially by the Pope. Unknown to Mary, Walsingham’s Catholic double agent Gilbert Gifford routed every coded letter smuggled inside **beer barrels** directly to Walsingham’s desk.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Master codebreaker **Thomas Phelippes** patiently deciphered every message until, on 17 July 1586, Mary dictated a reply explicitly endorsing the ‘dispatch’ (assassination) of Elizabeth before foreign troops landed. Phelippes forged a postscript requesting the six assassins’ names, enabling Walsingham to arrest Babington, execute the conspirators horribly, and seize Mary’s incriminating papers.",
