          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> In December 1577 Elizabeth secretly backed Drake’s expedition of five ships from Plymouth with orders to sail through the Strait of Magellan and raid Spanish Pacific possessions—while publicly claiming he was bound for Alexandria. Surviving fierce Magellan gales in his renamed flagship **Golden Hind**, Drake attacked unfortified Spanish ports up the coasts of Chile and Peru.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> In March 1579 Drake captured Spain’s premier Pacific treasure galleon, nicknamed the **Cacafuego**, seizing over £140,000 in silver bars, gold, and jewels before sailing across the Pacific and Indian oceans. Returning to Plymouth in September 1580 with roughly **£400,000** in total plunder, Drake gave Elizabeth enough Crown share to clear England’s entire national debt.",
