          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.1]</span> By 1584 indirect diplomacy collapsed altogether. Under the brilliant Spanish general **Duke of Parma**, Spain steadily reconquered southern Dutch towns; then on 10 July 1584 a Catholic assassin shot dead rebel leader William of Orange at Delft. Worse still, in December 1584 Philip II signed the **Treaty of Joinville** with the French Catholic League to eradicate Protestantism.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.2]</span> With France neutralised by Catholic League civil war and Antwerp falling to Parma, Elizabeth could no longer rely on surrogates. On 10 August 1585 she signed the **Treaty of Nonsuch** with the Dutch Protestant Estates, pledging 7,400 English soldiers under Robert Dudley, Earl of Leicester—an act Philip II treated as an open declaration of Anglo-Spanish war.",
