                "text": "<p>The English defeated the Spanish Armada in 1588 because English ships were much faster and had better cannons than the big, slow Spanish galleons. Also, the Spanish invasion plan went wrong when their fleet could not meet up properly with their soldiers waiting across the Channel.</p>",
                "verdict": "Level 1 (3/12) — Simple general points; needs specific Tudor facts, dates (e.g. Medina Sidonia, Parma, race-built galleons, 7 August Calais fireships), and 'because / this meant that' explanation."
