          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> Anchored off exposed **Calais Roads** on 6 August, Medina Sidonia learned to his dismay that Parma’s army at Dunkirk needed another week to embark and possessed no warships to clear Dutch blockaders. Seizing the moment around midnight on **7 August 1588**, Howard and Drake packed eight old vessels with pitch, brimstone, gunpowder, and double-shotted guns, setting these blazing **fireships** drifting on wind and tide toward the anchored Spaniards.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> Dreading catastrophic floating ‘hell-burners’ used previously against Spanish bridges at Antwerp, panic-stricken Spanish captains **cut anchor cables** in the darkness and scattered out into the open North Sea. Although not a single Spanish galleon burned that night, the Armada lost its primary heavy anchors and broke its disciplined crescent formation completely.",
