      "prologue": "Sixteenth-century England was a world where illiterate yeomen signed legal documents with a rough cross, yet boys as young as seven sat in freezing stone rooms chanting Latin grammar under the threat of the birch rod. Outside the classroom, Elizabethans gambled fortune on vicious bear-baiting pits before stepping into the open-air wooden playhouses of London to hear the secular thunder of Shakespeare and Marlowe. How did the Renaissance democratise English culture while reinforcing rigid social division?",
