          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Following the 1569 Northern Revolt, Parliament passed the **1572 Vagabonds Act** combining national welfare taxation with fierce physical deterrence. For the first time nationwide, local Justices of the Peace had to compile an official register of deserving poor and levy a weekly **compulsory poor rate** upon every wealthy parish householder—imprisoning anyone who refused to contribute.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Simultaneously, the 1572 statute imposed harsh corporal terror upon able-bodied vagrants aged over fourteen caught begging without a JP’s licence: first-time offenders were whipped naked through market towns and **bored through the ear** with a red-hot iron an inch thick; a second offence within sixty days meant hanging as a felon unless an employer hired them.",
          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Following the 1569 Northern Revolt, Parliament passed the **1572 Vagabonds Act** combining national welfare taxation with fierce physical deterrence. For the first time nationwide, local Justices of the Peace had to compile an official register of deserving poor and levy a weekly **compulsory poor rate** upon every wealthy parish householder—imprisoning anyone who refused to contribute.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Simultaneously, the 1572 statute imposed harsh corporal terror upon able-bodied vagrants aged over fourteen caught begging without a JP’s licence: first-time offenders were whipped naked through market towns and **bored through the ear** with a red-hot iron an inch thick; a second offence within sixty days meant hanging as a felon unless an employer hired them."
          ],
