          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> In December 1577 **Francis Drake** sailed from Plymouth with five vessels and 164 men—backed secretly by Elizabeth, Walsingham, and Leicester—to raid Spanish Pacific ports and avenge Spain’s 1568 treachery at San Juan de Ulúa. Surviving mutiny and ferocious storms through the **Strait of Magellan**, only Drake’s renamed flagship *Golden Hind* reached the Pacific in September 1578.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Sweeping north past unfortified Valparaíso and Callao, Drake captured the silver-laden *Cacafuego* before sailing up the North American coast in June 1579, where friendly Miwok people welcomed him and he claimed **Nova Albion** (‘New England’, likely California) for Queen Elizabeth. Crossing the Pacific, trading for cloves in the Moluccas, and rounding Africa, Drake reached Plymouth in September 1580.",
