          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.1]</span> Learning from 1585’s military mistakes, Raleigh sent artist-governor **John White** back in May 1587 with 118 men, women, and children—promised 500 acres per family—intending to settle deeper Chesapeake Bay, though their Portuguese master pilot Simon Fernandez landed them back on **Roanoke** Island, where loyal Manteo was christened Lord of Roanoke and White’s granddaughter Virginia Dare was born.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.2]</span> After hostile Algonquians killed colonist George Howe while crabbing, anxious settlers persuaded White to sail back to England for urgent supplies in August 1587. Tragically, the **1588 Spanish Armada** caused Elizabeth to requisition every seaworthy English vessel; when White finally returned in August 1590, Roanoke stood deserted with **‘CROATOAN’** carved into a palisade post—ending Elizabethan America.",
